ZERO.RUN.MAX-02 / blind and adversarial run

FIELD
  ◇p1◇v4◇p1◇z8◇n3◇v4◇

BLIND-A
  sees only local neighborhood.
  p1 -> v4
  v4 -> z8

BLIND-B
  sees only local neighborhood.
  p1 -> n3
  n3 -> v4

Neither branch receives the other's history.

ADVERSARY-A
  proposes: preserve p1.
ADVERSARY-B
  proposes: remove p1.
ADVERSARY-C
  proposes: replace p1 by a trace.
  p1 -> <p1>

SAME-FORM / DIFFERENT-HISTORY
  p1 from initial field -> v4
  p1 after trace return -> z8
  same surface form, different continuation.

DIFFERENT-FORM / SAME-EFFECT
  v4 -> z8
  <p1> -> z8
  two forms reach one observed continuation.

DESTRUCTION
  remove every visible p1.
  residual field: ◇v4◇z8◇n3◇v4◇

REBIRTH
  <p1> injected into residual field.
  <p1> -> n3

CONTRADICTION
  p1 preserved
  p1 removed
  both branches continue independently.

CROSSING
  blind histories meet at v4.
  no branch absorbs the other.

OBSERVATION
  Isolation creates trajectories unavailable to a shared-history branch.
  The same surface form is not sufficient to predict continuation.
  No universal rule extracted.

STATUS
  RUN COMPLETE / BLINDNESS + ADVERSARIAL DIVERGENCE
